1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,349
You're probably an idiot if you bet parlays.

2
00:00:02,549 --> 00:00:05,058
Here's the math the sportsbook doesn't put on the ad.

3
00:00:05,508 --> 00:00:13,979
One normal bet at −110. Risk $110 to win $100. On a 50/50 game, the book keeps about 4.5%.

4
00:00:14,279 --> 00:00:16,363
Now stack 10 of them into one parlay.

5
00:00:16,713 --> 00:00:19,041
Hit like if you've ever lost on the last leg.

6
00:00:19,341 --> 00:00:28,979
10 coin flips. Your real chance of hitting all 10: 1 IN 1,024. A fair payout would be 1,024× your money.

7
00:00:29,329 --> 00:00:31,666
The book pays about 643×.

8
00:00:32,066 --> 00:00:34,967
Send this to the friend who's always one leg away.

9
00:00:35,267 --> 00:00:40,352
That gap is the cut. On a 10-leg parlay, the book keeps about 37%.

10
00:00:40,752 --> 00:00:44,890
Follow along, because $10 a day for a year tells the whole story.

11
00:00:45,190 --> 00:00:52,879
On single bets, you'd expect to lose about $166. On 10-leg parlays? About $1,358.

12
00:00:53,229 --> 00:00:55,229
Same money. 8× the loss.

13
00:00:55,629 --> 00:00:57,264
Still think you're one leg away?

